SUMMARY:'Quin Chat\; Behind the Curtain - To Kill a Mockingbird
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 100 spots left\n
 Status: You are on Waitlist\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/e
 vents/203290\n\n6:00PM Reception\, 6:30PM Discussion\nExperience a behind
 -the-curtain look as The Huntington Theatre Company prepares to present t
 he first regional production of Aaron Sorkin’s acclaimed adaptation of 
 To Kill a Mockingbird. Artistic Director and Director of the production\, 
 Loretta Greco joins fellow members of the production to explore the art an
 d complexity of bringing Harper Lee’s enduring classic to the stage\, r
 evealing what audiences rarely see: the journey from script to stage\, the
  artistic decisions made along the way\, and the collaboration required to
  bring a production of this scale to life. Together\, they will consider 
 the delicate balance between honoring a story that has resonated for gener
 ations and embracing the creative freedom and fresh perspective that come 
 with a new interpretation.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved fo
 r members only. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be served.
  We kindly ask that all cancellations be made at least 24 hours prior to t
 he start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/203290
CATEGORIES:The Arts
