SUMMARY:90 Minutes of Innovation
LOCATION:The Pub
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 140 spots le
 ft\nStatus: You are on Waitlist\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.c
 om/events/203300\n\n1:00PM Program\, 2:30PM Networking\nWhat does it take 
 to challenge convention\, build what doesn’t yet exist\, and turn ambiti
 ous ideas into meaningful change? In the latest edition of 90 Minutes of I
 nnovation\, John Werner - venture capitalist\, MIT lecturer\, and Forbes A
 I columnist - sits down with Lauren Kuntz\, PhD\, Head of Market Analysis
  at ENGIE\, Gaiascope co-founder\, and founder of the Women’s Greatest A
 thlete.\n\nWith degrees in Physics and Mechanical Engineering from MIT and
  a PhD in Climate Science from Harvard\, Kuntz co-founded the Y Combinato
 r-backed energy forecasting startup Gaiascope\, using AI to advance renewa
 ble energy markets before its 2025 acquisition by ENGIE.\n\nKuntz has brou
 ght that same drive to the world of sport. A world-record holder in the 2
 0-event double decathlon and three-time All-American\, she founded World�
 ��s Greatest Athlete in 2024 and the Women’s Decathlon World Championshi
 ps to challenge one of track and field’s longstanding disparities: wh
 ile men have competed in the Olympic decathalon since 1912\, women never h
 ave. Now\, she is helping build the case for the women’s decathlon to f
 inally earn its place at the Olympic Games.\n\nTogether\, Werner and Kuntz
  will explore what it means to pursue ideas before there is a roadmap\, ch
 allenge deeply established systems\, and build something entirely new. Fr
 om rethinking the power grid to reimagining who gets to compete on the wor
 ld’s biggest stage\, expect a wide-ranging conversation about seeing wha
 t could be—and having the nerve to build it. \n\n*This event is complim
 entary and reserved for members only. Complimentary light bites and refr
 eshments will be served. We kindly ask that all cancellations be made at l
 east 24 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/203300
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
